  "markdown": "Services\n\n# Timorous Beasties installation in London\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 17 October 2026\n\nWe install Timorous Beasties papers. On the public record, we hung Tropical Clouded Leopard and Totem Damask, custom-printed as vinyl, through the 111 guest rooms across seven storeys of Hyde London City.\n\n[Discuss a Timorous Beasties installation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=service%3Atimorous-beasties-installer) [See the work](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/)\n\nWe install Timorous Beasties papers. The project on the public record is Hyde London City, the former Old Bailey Hotel. Mr Wallcover is not on maker recommended-installer lists: a maker’s name on this site means we installed that maker’s product on that project.\n\n## What was hung\n\nTwo Timorous Beasties designs, produced as custom-printed vinyl wallpaper: Totem Damask in Black & Blue on guest-room feature walls, and Tropical Clouded Leopard in Vanilla on headboard walls. The interior designers, Studio Moren, selected the designs. For the maker’s range, see [Timorous Beasties](https://www.timorousbeasties.com/).\n\n## How it hangs\n\nAs the case study records it: a sample room first, with the headboard panel shaped and set out behind the bed, then the finish, the setting out and the detailing repeated across the bedrooms.\n\n## On the public record\n\nHyde London City, the former Old Bailey Hotel: 111 guest rooms across seven storeys, in a Grade II-listed Victorian building, about two years on site from a finished sample room in November 2022. The case study below is the record, with its photographs.\n\n![Sample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/old-bailey-06-800.webp)\n\nThe sample room at Hyde London City: Tropical Clouded Leopard by Timorous Beasties, set out as a shaped headboard panel.Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.[View the Hyde London City (the Old Bailey Hotel) case study](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\n## On the public record\n\n[![Sample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/old-bailey-06-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nSample room at Hyde London City with a Timorous Beasties Tropical Clouded Leopard panel behind the bed.Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [Hyde London City (the Old Bailey Hotel)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nFull decorating package: decoration, specialist wallcoverings and window film, c. 2 years.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/old-bailey-hotel/)\n\nQuestions\n\n## Asked about Timorous Beasties installation\n\nIllustrative material studies\n\nPause motion\n\n### Is Mr Wallcover a Timorous Beasties approved installer?\n\nNo. Mr Wallcover is not on maker recommended-installer lists. We installed two Timorous Beasties designs across the bedrooms of Hyde London City. A maker's name on this site means we installed that maker's product on that project; it is not a maker approval, accreditation or endorsement.\n\n### Why was the Timorous Beasties pattern printed as vinyl?\n\nThe case study records it: vinyl lets the patterns stand up to the daily wear of a busy hotel while keeping their colour and detail. The designs were selected by the interior designers, Studio Moren.\n\n### How is a pattern like this set out across a hotel?\n\nSample room first. Our record at Hyde London City starts with a finished sample room in November 2022, with Tropical Clouded Leopard behind the bed as a shaped headboard panel. Agreeing the finish, the setting out and the detailing in one room first meant the rest could be repeated with confidence.\n",
